    "sourceWikitext": "{{recipesummary|category=Soup recipes|servings=4|time=1 hour|difficulty=2}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|American cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Vegetarian cuisine|Vegetarian Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Soups|Soups]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]] (canned is fine)\n* 4 cups [[cookbook:Cream|heavy cream]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|ground white pepper]]\n* ¼ tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ¼ tsp [[Cookbook:Garlic Powder|granulated garlic]]\n* ⅛ tsp [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# In a [[Cookbook:Blender|blender]] or [[Cookbook:Food Processor|food processor]], working in batches if necessary, [[Cookbook:Puree|puree]] tomatoes, cream, sugar, pepper, salt, garlic and cayenne.\n# Transfer soup to a [[Cookbook:saucepan|saucepan]] and bring to a [[Cookbook:Boil|boil]] over high heat.\n# Reduce heat and [[Cookbook:simmer|simmer]], stirring occasionally, until soup thickens, 20–30 minutes.\n# Serve hot.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Try [[Cookbook:Garnish|garnishing]] soup with cooked [[Cookbook:shrimp|shrimp]] or slices of [[Cookbook:sausage|andouille sausage]].\n\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using heavy cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic powder]]",
